# Tracer: exact visible axioms for the two explicit source trust boundaries
#
# `abstract_prop` declares an opaque predicate interface. It becomes one
# source-scoped, universe-polymorphic Lean axiom with exactly this arity; it
# does not assert any application of the predicate.
abstract_prop marked(x)

# Explicit `trust` is the only statement proof allowed to create a proposition
# axiom. This exact trusted FactId becomes one visible Lean axiom.
trust $marked(1)

# Ordinary replay cites the trusted source FactId and becomes a theorem, not a
# third axiom.
$marked(1)

# Boundaries:
# - abstract_prop unproved(x) followed by $unproved(1) is rejected by Litex;
# - an ordinary checked fact emits no axiom;
# - `-strict` intentionally rejects this explicit unsafe source file, while
#   the ordinary runner, compiler axiom audit, and real Lean kernel accept the
#   declared boundary exactly as written.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -runner -f lean/examples/25_ExplicitSourceAxioms.lit
# cargo test --release --test stmt_result_to_lean_compiler_tracers
# and cd lean && lake env lean examples/25_ExplicitSourceAxioms.lean
